cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use these tools in published work, please cite this repository and the accompanying paper."
type: software
title: "ap-audit: AP re-scoring tools for oriented ship detection under missing modalities"
abstract: >-
  Pure-Python tools that recompute average precision from exported prediction
  files under either the all-point or the 11-point interpolation rule, switch
  the recall denominator between the full ground-truth set and the subset that
  remains after doubly-missing samples are excluded, and score the same
  predictions against either optical or SAR annotations. Every number reported
  in the accompanying letter can be re-derived offline from a single prediction
  file; no training is required to reproduce a metric.
